From a73911bc00ca932a53389a079af79e1322e662c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:14:41 -1200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] platform/x86: asus-wmi: Fix use-after-free of kbd_led on
 removal

Since the keyboard backlight LED is registered from kbd_led_work, it goes
through devm_led_classdev_register() on the platform device. The LED is
embedded in struct asus_wmi, which asus_wmi_remove() frees with kfree()
before the driver core releases the device's devres, so the LED core then
unregisters an LED that lives in freed memory. Unloading asus-nb-wmi after
a keyboard backlight listener made asus-wmi register the LED:

  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000008
  RIP: 0010:led_classdev_unregister+0x95/0xf0
  Call Trace:
   release_nodes+0x3a/0x60
   devres_release_all+0x86/0xc0
   device_unbind_cleanup+0x21/0xa0
   device_release_driver_internal+0x1bf/0x200
   bus_remove_device+0xdb/0x170
   device_del+0x15d/0x4a0
   platform_device_del.part.0+0xe/0x70
   platform_device_unregister+0x1b/0x30
   asus_wmi_unregister_driver+0x2c/0x50 [asus_wmi]
   __do_sys_delete_module+0x1cc/0x2c0

Register the LED with led_classdev_register() and unregister it in
asus_wmi_led_exit(), after the workqueue that registers it is destroyed.

Fixes: fac55d29581f ("platform/x86: asus-wmi: Add support for multiple kbd led handlers")
---
 drivers/platform/x86/asus-wmi.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/asus-wmi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/asus-wmi.c
index 6914f3cb0..6aacca85b 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/asus-wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/asus-wmi.c
@@ -1817,8 +1817,7 @@ static void kbd_led_update_all(struct work_struct *work)
 		 * Therefore, we can safely register the LED without holding
 		 * a spinlock.
 		 */
-		ret = devm_led_classdev_register(&asus->platform_device->dev,
-						 &asus->kbd_led);
+		ret = led_classdev_register(&asus->platform_device->dev, &asus->kbd_led);
 		if (!ret) {
 			scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &asus_ref.lock)
 				asus->kbd_led_registered = true;
@@ -2132,6 +2131,10 @@ static void asus_wmi_led_exit(struct asus_wmi *asus)
 
 	if (asus->led_workqueue)
 		destroy_workqueue(asus->led_workqueue);
+
+	/* kbd_led is registered from that workqueue, so it is settled only now */
+	if (asus->kbd_led_registered)
+		led_classdev_unregister(&asus->kbd_led);
 }
 
 static int asus_wmi_led_init(struct asus_wmi *asus)
-- 
